#: ../../source/api/events.md:1
msgid "Events"
msgstr "Events"

#: ../../source/api/events.md:3
msgid ""
"Events are methods that Miniworlds calls automatically. Register them on "
"a `World` or an `Actor` with the `@...register` decorator."
msgstr ""
"Events sind Methoden, die Miniworlds automatisch aufruft. Registriere sie"
" mit dem Decorator `@...register` an einer `World` oder einem `Actor`."

#: ../../source/api/events.md:6
msgid "Main Loop"
msgstr "Hauptschleife"

#: ../../source/api/events.md:18
msgid ""
"`on_setup` runs once before the world starts. `act` runs once per frame "
"while the world is running."
msgstr ""
"`on_setup` läuft einmal, bevor die Welt startet. `act` läuft einmal pro "
"Frame, solange die Welt läuft."

#: ../../source/api/events.md:21
msgid "Keyboard"
msgstr "Tastatur"

#: ../../source/api/events.md:23
msgid "Use a specific key handler when you only care about one key:"
msgstr ""
"Verwende einen tastenspezifischen Handler, wenn dich nur eine Taste "
"interessiert:"

#: ../../source/api/events.md:35
msgid "Use a generic handler when you need to inspect the currently pressed keys:"
msgstr ""
"Verwende einen allgemeinen Handler, wenn du die aktuell gedrückten Tasten"
" auswerten musst:"

#: ../../source/api/events.md:46
msgid "Keyboard events:"
msgstr "Tastatur-Events:"

#: ../../source/api/events.md:48
msgid "`on_key_down(self, keys)`: once when a key is pressed"
msgstr "`on_key_down(self, keys)`: einmal, wenn eine Taste gedrückt wird"

#: ../../source/api/events.md:49
msgid "`on_key_pressed(self, keys)`: every frame while a key is held"
msgstr ""
"`on_key_pressed(self, keys)`: in jedem Frame, solange eine Taste gehalten"
" wird"

#: ../../source/api/events.md:50
msgid "`on_key_up(self, keys)`: when a key is released"
msgstr "`on_key_up(self, keys)`: wenn eine Taste losgelassen wird"

#: ../../source/api/events.md:51
msgid ""
"`on_key_down_<key>(self)`, `on_key_pressed_<key>(self)`, "
"`on_key_up_<key>(self)`: key-specific handlers without a `keys` parameter"
msgstr ""
"`on_key_down_<key>(self)`, `on_key_pressed_<key>(self)`, "
"`on_key_up_<key>(self)`: tastenspezifische Handler ohne `keys`-Parameter"

#: ../../source/api/events.md:53
msgid ""
"`on_text_input(self, text)`: composed text (including umlauts and "
"spaces); use this for text entry, e.g. inside an `Input` widget"
msgstr ""
"`on_text_input(self, text)`: zusammengesetzter Text (einschließlich "
"Umlauten und Leerzeichen); verwende dies für Texteingaben, z. B. in einem"
" `Input`-Widget"

#: ../../source/api/events.md:56
msgid ""
"Common key names include `w`, `a`, `s`, `d`, `space`, `left`, `right`, "
"`up`, and `down`."
msgstr ""
"Gängige Tastennamen sind `w`, `a`, `s`, `d`, `space`, `left`, `right`, "
"`up` und `down`."

#: ../../source/api/events.md:59
msgid "Mouse"
msgstr "Maus"

#: ../../source/api/events.md:72
msgid "Mouse events:"
msgstr "Maus-Events:"

#: ../../source/api/events.md:74
msgid ""
"`on_mouse_left(self, position)`, `on_mouse_right(self, position)`, "
"`on_mouse_middle(self, position)`: while a button is held"
msgstr ""
"`on_mouse_left(self, position)`, `on_mouse_right(self, position)`, "
"`on_mouse_middle(self, position)`: solange eine Taste gehalten wird"

#: ../../source/api/events.md:76
msgid ""
"`on_mouse_left_down(self, position)`, `on_mouse_left_up(self, position)`:"
" press and release events"
msgstr ""
"`on_mouse_left_down(self, position)`, `on_mouse_left_up(self, position)`:"
" Drücken und Loslassen"

#: ../../source/api/events.md:78
msgid "`on_mouse_motion(self, position)`: mouse movement"
msgstr "`on_mouse_motion(self, position)`: Mausbewegung"

#: ../../source/api/events.md:79
msgid ""
"`on_clicked(self, position)`, `on_clicked_left(self, position)`, "
"`on_clicked_right(self, position)`: actor click events"
msgstr ""
"`on_clicked(self, position)`, `on_clicked_left(self, position)`, "
"`on_clicked_right(self, position)`: Klick-Events für Actors"

#: ../../source/api/events.md:81
msgid ""
"`on_mouse_over(self, position)`, `on_mouse_enter(self, position)`, "
"`on_mouse_leave(self, position)`: actor hover events"
msgstr ""
"`on_mouse_over(self, position)`, `on_mouse_enter(self, position)`, "
"`on_mouse_leave(self, position)`: Hover-Events für Actors"

#: ../../source/api/events.md:83
msgid ""
"`on_wheel_up(self, position)`, `on_wheel_down(self, position)`: mouse "
"wheel"
msgstr "`on_wheel_up(self, position)`, `on_wheel_down(self, position)`: Mausrad"

#: ../../source/api/events.md:84
msgid ""
"`on_tile_enter(self, tile)`, `on_tile_leave(self, tile)`: the mouse "
"enters or leaves a hex (`HexWorld` only)"
msgstr ""
"`on_tile_enter(self, tile)`, `on_tile_leave(self, tile)`: die Maus "
"betritt oder verlässt ein Hexfeld (nur `HexWorld`)"

#: ../../source/api/events.md:87
msgid "Sensors And Borders"
msgstr "Sensoren und Ränder"

#: ../../source/api/events.md:99
msgid "Sensor and collision events:"
msgstr "Sensor- und Kollisions-Events:"

#: ../../source/api/events.md:101
msgid "`on_detecting(self, other)`: any detected actor"
msgstr "`on_detecting(self, other)`: irgendein erkannter Actor"

#: ../../source/api/events.md:102
msgid "`on_detecting_actor(self, other)`: any actor on the same position"
msgstr "`on_detecting_actor(self, other)`: irgendein Actor auf derselben Position"

#: ../../source/api/events.md:103
msgid ""
"`on_detecting_<ClassName>(self, other)`: actors of a specific class, for "
"example `on_detecting_wall`"
msgstr ""
"`on_detecting_<ClassName>(self, other)`: Actors einer bestimmten Klasse, "
"zum Beispiel `on_detecting_wall`"

#: ../../source/api/events.md:105
msgid "`on_not_detecting(self)`: no actor detected"
msgstr "`on_not_detecting(self)`: kein Actor erkannt"

#: ../../source/api/events.md:106
msgid "`on_not_detecting_<ClassName>(self)`: no actor of that class detected"
msgstr "`on_not_detecting_<ClassName>(self)`: kein Actor dieser Klasse erkannt"

#: ../../source/api/events.md:107
msgid "`on_detecting_world(self)`: actor is inside the world"
msgstr "`on_detecting_world(self)`: der Actor befindet sich in der Welt"

#: ../../source/api/events.md:108
msgid "`on_not_detecting_world(self)`: actor is outside the world"
msgstr "`on_not_detecting_world(self)`: der Actor befindet sich außerhalb der Welt"

#: ../../source/api/events.md:109
msgid "`on_detecting_not_on_world(self)`: alias for `on_not_detecting_world`"
msgstr "`on_detecting_not_on_world(self)`: Alias für `on_not_detecting_world`"

#: ../../source/api/events.md:110
msgid "`on_detecting_borders(self, borders)`: receives a list like `[\"left\"]`"
msgstr "`on_detecting_borders(self, borders)`: erhält eine Liste wie `[\"left\"]`"

#: ../../source/api/events.md:111
msgid ""
"`on_detecting_left_border(self)`, `on_detecting_right_border(self)`, "
"`on_detecting_top_border(self)`, `on_detecting_bottom_border(self)`"
msgstr ""
"`on_detecting_left_border(self)`, `on_detecting_right_border(self)`, "
"`on_detecting_top_border(self)`, `on_detecting_bottom_border(self)`"

#: ../../source/api/events.md:114
msgid ""
"Both `on_not_detecting_world` and `on_detecting_not_on_world` are "
"accepted."
msgstr ""
"Sowohl `on_not_detecting_world` als auch `on_detecting_not_on_world` "
"werden akzeptiert."

#: ../../source/api/events.md:116
msgid "Messages"
msgstr "Nachrichten"

#: ../../source/api/events.md:118
msgid ""
"Messages are useful when actors should communicate without holding direct"
" references to each other."
msgstr ""
"Nachrichten sind nützlich, wenn Actors miteinander kommunizieren sollen, "
"ohne direkte Verweise aufeinander zu halten."

#: ../../source/api/events.md:131
msgid ""
"Use `send_message(message, data=None)` to broadcast a message. Use "
"`@actor.register_message(\"message\")` or "
"`@world.register_message(\"message\")` to react to it."
msgstr ""
"Verwende `send_message(message, data=None)`, um eine Nachricht zu senden."
" Mit `@actor.register_message(\"message\")` oder "
"`@world.register_message(\"message\")` reagierst du darauf."

#: ../../source/api/events.md:135
msgid "Focus"
msgstr "Fokus"

#: ../../source/api/events.md:137
msgid "Actors can react when they receive or lose focus after a click:"
msgstr ""
"Actors können reagieren, wenn sie nach einem Klick den Fokus erhalten "
"oder verlieren:"

#: ../../source/api/events.md:139
msgid "`on_focus(self)`"
msgstr "`on_focus(self)`"

#: ../../source/api/events.md:140
msgid "`on_focus_lost(self)`"
msgstr "`on_focus_lost(self)`"

